--TEST--
`bindTo`, `bind` and `call` give a closure a new `$this` of its own class or a subclass, and a closure that does not use `$this` comes back unchanged — `rule:types/callable-is-the-only-function-type`, `rule:statements/an-anonymous-function-captures-this-only-where-it-uses-it`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Counter {
    public int $n;

    public function constructor(int $n) {
        $this->n = $n;
    }

    public function reader(): callable(): int {
        return fn (): int => $this->n;
    }

    // A closure inside a closure: the inner one also uses `$this`.
    public function nested(): callable(): callable {
        return fn (): callable => fn (): int => $this->n * 10;
    }
}

class BigCounter extends Counter {}

class Other {
    public int $n = 99;
}

Counter $one = new Counter(1);
Counter $two = new Counter(2);
callable(): int $read = $one->reader();

// The copy reads the new object. The original still reads the old one.
callable(): int $readTwo = $read->bindTo($two);
echo $readTwo(), " ", $read(), "\n";

// `bind` is the same operation. A subclass has the same properties.
echo $read->bind(new BigCounter(3))(), "\n";

// `call` binds and calls in one step.
echo $read->call($two), "\n";

callable $inner = $one->nested()();
echo $inner->bindTo($two)(), "\n";

// A closure that does not use `$this` comes back unchanged, whatever it is bound to.
callable $add = fn (int $x, int $y): int => $x + $y;
echo $add->bindTo(new Other())(1, 2), " ", $add->bindTo(null)(3, 4), "\n";
echo $add->call(new Other(), 5, 6), "\n";
array<int> $pair = [7, 8];
echo $add->call(null, ...$pair), "\n";

// `?->` gives `null` when there is no closure.
?callable $none = null;
echo $none?->bindTo($two) == null ? "null" : "a closure", "\n";

// An object of an unrelated class, and `null`, are refused for a closure that uses `$this`.
try {
    $read->bindTo(new Other());
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $read->call(null);
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
2 1
3
2
20
3 7
11
15
null
this closure uses `$this`, so it can only be bound to an object of class `Counter` or a subclass of it. The argument is an object of class `Other`
this closure uses `$this`, so it can only be bound to an object of class `Counter` or a subclass of it. The argument is `null`
